# 0-fault clusters of the hot group (LAYOUT-TEXT-PIN, D-X.63): <name> TAB <first key> TAB <last key>.
# Hand-kept (hot-text.list is generated). A cluster is every list position from its first key to its
# last; `cargo xtask so` aligns its first section to the smallest power of two not below its size, so
# it never straddles a 64 KiB fault-around window. Each starts with a function the earlier calls of its
# probe mode (page_faults.c) already ran, so the later call finds its text in a touched window.
# time: localtime_r's conversion (local_in) to the code only the first mktime runs (mode mktime).
# strings: the string kernels to the printf entry that runs first (mode strings); the printf body after it
# (vfprintf ...) is start-up text, at the list head since ruling #4417 (LAYOUT-TEXT-PIN-5); so is memmove,
# which start-up reaches through its entry labels (merge.py --alias, #4467, LAYOUT-TEXT-PIN-6). It ends at
# liella_hot_memchr_rest (HEAP-FIRST-USE-6): the folding decision is lazy (D-3.20), so the mode's first memchr
# runs the checked rest path, which p_strlazy first touches after its printf.
# rebind: bindtextdomain to the catalog lookup and the same-text check of a rebind (mode rebind), in two
# clusters of at most 32 KiB each (rebind, rebind-tail from catalog_of): one 38 KiB cluster took a 64 KiB
# alignment, which moved .text's start by 60 KiB and cost 52 KiB of gap ahead of it (ruling #4363).
# float: the first float conversion (mode float).
# @place end (LAYOUT-TEXT-PIN-4): the clusters, in this file's order, follow the last list position, so no
# alignment gap falls among the start-up and plain text (STARTUP-TEXT-WINDOWS) and the gaps sit side by
# side; largest alignment first (float, 16 KiB in the fast profile, last). `@place	in-place` keeps them at
# their list positions.
@place	end
